# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE BROWSER'S HALF
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values from your Supabase project
# (Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API)
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is git-ignored. Never commit real keys.
#
# Everything here is PUBLIC. Vite bakes every VITE_ variable into the bundle it
# ships, so a secret in this file is a secret on a web page. The anon key is
# meant to be public and row-level security is what protects the data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SERVER'S HALF, which does NOT belong in this file
#
# Billing needs secrets, and secrets cannot live in a Vite build. They are set
# on the Edge Functions instead, where no browser can read them:
#
#   supabase secrets set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=rk_live_...
#   supabase secrets set STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
#   supabase secrets set STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=price_...
#   supabase secrets set SITE_URL=https://your-site.example
#
# Optional, and off unless set to exactly "true":
#
#   STRIPE_PRICE_YEARLY        a second price, once you make one in Stripe
#   STRIPE_MANAGED_PAYMENTS    make Stripe the merchant of record for the sale.
#                              Accepting the terms in the Dashboard is NOT
#                              enough on its own: the Checkout Session has to
#                              ask for it too, and this flag is what asks
#   STRIPE_AUTOMATIC_TAX       for selling as your own merchant of record with
#                              a Stripe Tax registration. Ignored when the flag
#                              above is on, because then Stripe is the seller
#                              and handles the tax itself
#   STRIPE_REQUIRE_TOS         show the terms tickbox at checkout. Needs a terms
#                              URL saved under the Stripe account's public details
#   STRIPE_CANCEL_ON_DISPUTE   cancel a subscription automatically when a
#                              chargeback is opened against it
#
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected
# into every function by the platform. Do not set them by hand and never copy
# the service role key anywhere else: it bypasses every policy in the database.
#
# See README.md, "Taking money", for the whole setup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
